---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_URL } from "../lib/site";
import { breadcrumbLd, type Crumb } from "../lib/schema";

const crumbs: Crumb[] = [
  { name: "Home", href: "/" },
  { name: "How we research", href: "/how-we-research/" },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How We Research & Score Dehumidifiers"
  description={`How ${SITE_NAME} researches whole-house dehumidifiers: where our specs come from, how the 10-point score works, how we handle AHAM vs saturation ratings, and how often guides are updated.`}
  canonical={`${SITE_URL}/how-we-research/`}
  jsonLd={breadcrumbLd(crumbs)}
>
  <div class="wrap post-wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>How we research and score dehumidifiers</h1>
      <p class="lead-p">
        We'd rather tell you exactly how our recommendations are made than imply something they
        aren't. Here's the process behind every guide, review and calculator on {SITE_NAME}.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do (and don't do)</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE_NAME} is a <strong>research-based</strong> buyer's guide. We don't run a lab, and our
        reviews are not hands-on tests. Instead, for every model we:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Start from the manufacturer's spec sheet</strong>: AHAM capacity, coverage, drainage, dimensions, power draw, filter type, warranty.</li>
        <li><strong>Translate the marketing.</strong> Some brands advertise "saturation" capacity measured near 90°F/90% RH — roughly double the comparable AHAM figure. We always lead with the AHAM number and label the box number for what it is.</li>
        <li><strong>Cross-check with independent reviews</strong> from publications that do test hands-on, and note where their results differ from the marketing claims.</li>
        <li><strong>Read owner reports</strong> (forums, retailer reviews, support threads) for the problems that only show up after months of use: drain clogs, pump failures, noise complaints, support response times.</li>
        <li><strong>Flag uncertainty.</strong> When a spec can't be confirmed, or sources disagree, we say so rather than guess.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Each model page lists the sources we relied on.</p>

      <h2>How the 10-point score works</h2>
      <p>Every model gets four sub-scores, each out of 10:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Capacity</strong>: honest AHAM pints/day relative to the unit's size class and rated coverage.</li>
        <li><strong>Efficiency</strong>: energy factor (L/kWh), amp draw and Energy Star status — what it costs to run.</li>
        <li><strong>Build quality</strong>: cabinet construction, coil protection, filter quality, warranty length and brand support reputation.</li>
        <li><strong>Value</strong>: typical street price against what you get, including warranty and running costs.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The overall score is a weighted blend of the four, rounded to one decimal, plus small adjustments for
        reliability and support reputation. A 9+ is exceptional, 8–9 is a strong buy for the right space,
        and under 7.5 means real compromises.
      </p>
      <p>
        A higher score doesn't mean it's the right unit for <em>you</em>. A 9.0 whole-house flagship is a bad buy for a
        1,000 sq ft crawl space. That's why we built the <a href="/tools/capacity-sizer/">capacity sizer</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Prices</h2>
      <p>
        Prices are typical US street prices at the time of our last update and are shown as ranges because
        dehumidifiers are discounted often. Always check the current price on the retailer page.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate links and independence</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE_NAME} is reader-supported. As an Amazon Associate we earn from qualifying purchases made through
        our links, at no extra cost to you. Commissions never decide which products we recommend or how they
        are ranked. Brands cannot pay for placement, and we don't accept free products in exchange for coverage.
      </p>

      <h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        We review our main buying guides at least quarterly and whenever a significant
        model launches. Each page shows its last-updated date. Spot an error? <a href="/contact/">Tell us</a>
        and we'll fix it.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
